**File: `.claude/helpers/metrics-db.mjs:258-282`**

`syncMetrics()` issues one `db.run()` per module directory inside a loop. With N modules, that's N separate write transactions. sql.js has no autocommit batching.

```js
// CURRENT — N separate transactions
for (const entry of entries) {
  if (entry.isDirectory() && ...) {
    db.run(`INSERT OR REPLACE INTO module_status (...) VALUES (?, ...)`, [...]);
  }
}
persist();
```

```js
// FIX — wrap in a single transaction
db.run('BEGIN');
for (const entry of entries) {
  if (entry.isDirectory() && ...) {
    db.run(`INSERT OR REPLACE INTO module_status (...) VALUES (?, ...)`, [...]);
  }
}
db.run('COMMIT');
persist();
```

**Same file, lines 324-326** — three individual CVE updates could be one statement:

```js
// CURRENT
db.run("UPDATE cve_status SET status = ?, last_updated = ? WHERE id = 'CVE-1'", [...]);
db.run("UPDATE cve_status SET status = ?, last_updated = ? WHERE id = 'CVE-2'", [...]);
db.run("UPDATE cve_status SET status = ?, last_updated = ? WHERE id = 'CVE-3'", [...]);

// FIX — parameterize in a loop inside the same transaction opened above
for (const [id, fixed] of [['CVE-1', cve1Fixed], ['CVE-2', cve2Fixed], ['CVE-3', cve3Fixed]]) {
  db.run("UPDATE cve_status SET status = ?, last_updated = ? WHERE id = ?",
    [fixed ? 'fixed' : 'pending', now, id]);
}
```

