**File: `.claude/helpers/intelligence.cjs:519-522`**

`getContext()` is called on every `UserPromptSubmit` hook. It recomputes `trigrams(entry.words)` for every ranked entry on every call — O(entries × tokens) work that is already available from `init()`.

```js
// CURRENT — trigrams recomputed every query
for (const entry of ranked.entries) {
  const entryTrigrams = trigrams(entry.words || []);
  const contentMatch = jaccardSimilarity(promptTrigrams, entryTrigrams);
  ...
}
```

The fix is to store the trigram set at `init()` time in `ranked-context.json` alongside `words`:

```js
// In init() — lines 464-483, add trigrams to each rankedEntry:
const rankedEntries = deduped.map(entry => {
  const words = tokenize(content + ' ' + summary);
  return {
    ...entry,
    words,
    wordTrigrams: Array.from(trigrams(words)),  // precompute once
  };
});
```

```js
// In getContext() — read precomputed set instead of recomputing:
for (const entry of ranked.entries) {
  const entryTrigrams = new Set(entry.wordTrigrams || []);  // O(k) construction, no recomputation
  const contentMatch = jaccardSimilarity(promptTrigrams, entryTrigrams);
  ...
}
```

